<title>FINLAND: FINNISH FEB BUILDING PERMITS DOWN ONE-FIFTH - SF.</title>
<headline>FINNISH FEB BUILDING PERMITS DOWN ONE-FIFTH - SF.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The construction volume for which new building permits were granted fell by about a fifth year-on-year in February to 1.7 million cubic metres, Statistics Finland (SF) said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>However, the total number of permits for housing construction were up sharply: &quot;Building permits were granted in February for more than 2,400 new dwellings, or twice as many as a year earlier,&quot; SF said.</p>
<p>In January-February, the total construction volume for which building permits were granted rose nine percent year-on-year to 3.37 million cubic metres, SF said.</p>
</text>
